**Topic**
As the title said, I wanted to implement a custom command but I think I'm overstepping the mark - can you smack me back down to earth

**Your thoughts**
- I don't know go
- I wanted to choose a way to delete remote branches associated with a local branch via a custom command
- I can maybe do this through the 'Remotes' pane but we have literally 10,000 remotes because people forget to clean up and scrolling through them is tedious at best

So I came up with the basic scenario of:
```
  - key: '<c-d>'
    command: 'git push origin :{{.SelectedLocalBranch.Name}}'
    context: 'localBranches'
    description: 'delete remote branch of this local branch'
```
which is fine but a bit dangerous. I just want to delete branches that I am responsible for and have a list of protected branches. And also a dummies prompt which may annoy me in time but may also save me from accidentally destroying something.

Promise not to laugh, but here's the pseudocode I wanted to kinda work:
```
  - key: '<c-d>'
    command: '
      {{$response := index .PromptResponses 0}}
      {{$lowercase_delete := eq $response "y"}}
      {{$uppercase_delete := eq $response "Y"}}
      {{$delete := or $lowercase_delete $uppercase_delete}}
      {{if $delete}}
        {{$protected_branches := []string{"protected_branch_1", "protected_branch_2", "protected_branch_3"}}}
        {{$dont_delete := true}}
        {{
          for i := 0; i < $protected_branches.Len(); i++ {
            if eq $protected_branches.Index(i) .SelectedLocalBranch.Name {
              $dont_delete := true
            }
          }
        }}
        {{if not $dont_delete}}
          git push origin :{{.SelectedLocalBranch.Name}}
        {{end}}
      {{end}}'
    context: 'localBranches'
    description: 'delete remote branch of this local branch'
    prompts:
      - type: 'input'
        title: 'Are you sure?'
        initialValue: 'n'
```
